        <p>BOWLING,</p>
        <p>BRITISH CROWN GREEN ASSOCIATION</p>
        <p>INDIVIDUAL MERIT CHAMPIONSHIP. SUCCESS OF A LEIESEURE PLAYER. Eight of the prize-winners in each county where individual merit competitions have taken place should have turned out in this championship contest at 31413e1d on Monday, but owing to only two players putting in an appearance from Warwick and Worcester, the committee had to re-arrange the first round. Considering that the players from a distance had had no previous acquaintance with the green, and that some of the Yorkshire competitors had had the advantage of bowling on the enclosure on n:any occasions, great credit is due to the finalists—Rosa and Dale—for the se:coons they achieved. Rosa had not the slightest hope of success, as be only commenced bowling in earnest last season, out he played his games in fine style, and in the final the players were It) all at one stage. Dale's victory was a popular one and thoroughly deserved. Details :</p>
