        <p>ton (35); 3, Joseph Dovey, Whines P.A.C. (CO). Heat 2: 1, II Burden, Warrington (40) ; 2, J W Bond, Wigan (15) ; 3, Joseph Maloney, Manchester (35). After tluk first two laps of the final, there were only four men who had a chance and these kept close together. When the last lap was entered upon, it was wheel to wheel. Maloney, however, had been reserving himself sod a quarter of the way round topped saddle and gained about three lengths on the other, to win easily from Burden, who secured the second position from Swift. Ilalf-mile Handicap.—There were 30 competitors in this race, which was a most exciting ens. 1131 brook (46) who was considered a likely local, dropped out through an aecident fifty yards from home. There was a good pack on the last lap but T 0 Donoghue, Liver- pool (67), made good headway, showing remarkable stamina, and won in line style, xith E Ince, Widnes (38), second, and 'l' Wall, %Van-1111;ton (70), third. There was nothing much to choose between the second and third men and Wall had forged ahead wonderfully on the last round.</p>
        <p>_ One Mile Bicycle Handicap.—Heat 1 : 1, Charles Hutton' Widnes (170) ; 3 G Clare, Risley (135). Heat 2: 1, Frederick Shtdwell, Warrington A.C. (1751 ; 2, John Campbell, St Helens C.C. (130) Heat 3 : 1, 3 if Ardern, High Leigh (130) ; 2, Robert Monks, Earlestown (150). In the final the men were soon on fairly even terms, but on the last two laps it was neck and neck between Campbell, Clare and Arden). On the last lap Ardern seemed to have tie race well in hand but Campbell paced him well and 200 )ards from the pout the St Helens man was a length ahead. Ardern gradually gair.ed and inch by inch he crept up and only finished a wheel behind Campbell. Claie, v.ho R Ali a strong favourite for this rHce, ran third.</p>
        <p>200 .-Yards Handicap.— Heat 1: 1, IN Bryan, Birken- head (17). Heat 2 : 1, S Green, Salford (13i). Heat 3 : 1, J A J•ines, Birkenhead (18). Heat 4 : 1, fl Povey, Warrington A.C. (15). . Heat 5: 1, J H Foster, Black- pool (16). Heat. 6 : 8 Poizer, Ardwick (16). The local man Povey was well away trom the start in the final and gained a good lend ',which he maintained until the end, when he cleated the tapes over a 3 ard in front of 13.3 an who just pulleo away from the third man Porter. Two competitors had a nasty tall quite near home, although they were not seriously</p>
