      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1912-08-10_WidnesExaminer_art0030" n="art0030">
        <head>WARRINGTON AND DISTRICT BOWLING</head>
        <p>WARRINGTON AND DISTRICT BOWLING</p>
        <p>ASSOCIATION.</p>
        <p>Individual Merit Competition.</p>
        <p>The competition was continued on the Cemetery Hotel green on Saturday. the green being in splendid condition. Rain fell in the later stages of the day, and progress was suspended until Monday. Details:— SECOND ROUND (Continued). N Fielding, Cemetery 21 T Bridge, Cemetery ... 11 W Roughly, Rylands... 21 J Melbourne, Cem... 18 J Bowyer, l'eu;soth... w.o. W Butterworth, C... aim. C Jordan, Cemetery ... 21 S Robinson, Cemetery 17 _ THIRD ROUND. . _ _</p>
        <p>J W Jolley, Bulls Head 21 J Bowyer, Penketh ... 14 A Warburton, Worms 2l T Quarrie Cemetery... 20 A Foster, Cemetery E Taylor, Sea Con 1 C Jordan, Cemetery... 11 E Gleave, Cemetery A Scott, Cemetery 2l H Hughes, Sea Con ... 17 R Sunderland, Jun Con 21 J Howarth, Cemetery 7 R Holbrook, Jun Con H Williams, Rylands 2l F Miller, Rylands G Ball, jun, Cemetery ... 21 H Eyes, Rylands J Bate, Bolls Head 2l T Cooper, Sen Con ... 15 J Holland, Sen Con 11 F Anderton, Sen Con 21 T Humphreys' Ryrds 18 T Ellison, Whiteoross FOURTH ROUND.</p>
        <p>N Fielding — 'if -ii-die.ave J Holland 2l A Scott lB H Williams J W Jolley 0 Ball, jun 2l J Bate T Ellison E Taylor A Foster, a bye</p>
