        <p>DRAWINGS. COLOUR DRAWINGS.</p>
        <p>_ Ages 8, 10.-1, Alice Acton; 2, Dorothea Cobley. Ages 10, 12.-1, Harry Scott ; 2, Arthur Goodwin. Ages 12. 15.-1, Harold Short; 2, John lirandwood. PENCIL AND PEN DRAWINGS. Ages 8. 10.-1, Lucy Gerrard: 2, 111-sry Smith. Ages 10, 12.-1, James Lyall ; 2, Hernaie 51awson. Age3'l2, 15.-1, Ruth Vaxvson; 2, Sam Gleave. SPORTS. Stamp licking race.-1, B V Jenkins. Obstacle race.-1, li Boyle ;2, F Caldwell ;3, A Sankey. Bicycle egg and spoon race.—l, W Hill ;2, L. Vernon. Wheelbarrow race (girls).-1, J Dunlop: 2,L Gerrard Pillow Light on pole.-1, A Sandford ; 2, W. Clarke.</p>
        <p>THE GARDEN COMPETITION. The judges of gardens, Messrs R Poulton and William Yarwood report as follows:—" We have carefully judged all the gardens and other exhibits entered in the above competition and wish to congratulate all competitors who have been successful in winning prizes, and also those who are not in the prize list, as we consider practically all the competitors merit great praise for the skill and attention they have shown in the cultiva- tion of vegetables and flowers. We neticed in several gardens where roses were well grown that the blooms were past their best, and if these gardens had been judged a week or a fortnight earlier many more points would have been gained, which leads Us to suggest that the competition might he held with advantage rather earlier in the season. In class five much skill and taste are shown in the cultivation of backyard gardens and they form a very pleasing feature of the competition. In class seven, the neatest and best stocked greenhouse, we specially recommend the only exhibitor (No. 23) for a perfect example of a well kept and well stocked greenhouse in which numerous varieties of choice plants are well grown and arranged with good taste and which at the time of judging were a mass of bloom. Mucus improvement is shown in the juvenile classes, especially in class 12. The competitors in class 11 deserve every encourage- ment and we heartily commend all exhibitors in these , two classes.</p>
      </div>
