        <p>DARESBURY RIFLE CLUB v APPLETON RIFLE</p>
        <p>CLUB. The Appleton Club visited the former club's range on Saturday. The weather remained fine, though dull, until just before the finish of the match. The light was fairly good for shooting. The conditions were : Ten men aside, the best eight scores ta count ; seven shots and one sighting shot, at a decimal target, at 25, 50, and 100 yards ; possible score at each range, 70. The match throughout was very keenly contested, and as will he seen from the results given below, the Appleton team proved victors by thirteen points, The Darestury Club kindly provided tea on the range. DARESBURY. 25yd3. 50yds. 100yds. Total. II Potts, jun J Grosvenor,capt 65 65 68 198 B Ryder 67 61 67 198 S Whitlow 67 68 62 197 J Ryder 65 65 61 194 G Wallworth 66 63 63 152 I J Ravenscroft G Tickle 67 62 60 189</p>
