        <p>Risley. ENDENT METHODIST CHURCH.—The ennirer sermons were preached on Sunday by Mr. William of Leigh. Fair congregations were in attend- spite of the inclement weather.—ln the after- ft very helpful address was given by Mr. Bellamy lacholars and friends, the subject being " The IR for pleasure." Solos, duets and recitations `ndered, and a very helpful time was spent. The )ns amounted to .£4.</p>
        <p>Stockton Heath. L'ReFT DEFENCE.—St. Thomas's, Stockton Heath, Monthly says :—Those who signed our local ,a to Parliament objecting to the disendowment Church in Wales will be interested to know that ltures totalled 1,133, although the time allowed collectors was comparatively short. Our IS now in London, and will form part of the number which will shortly be presented to</p>
        <p>Frodsham. t, cft -,RET CLUB SPORTS.—The sports promoted by tbe hilla Cricket Club are always a popular Bank 'Y attraction and a large crowd witnessed an</p>
        <p>~.ng series of contests on Monday. The entries ghtly less then last year. Mrs Winslow pre- the prizes at the close. Results : Yards youths' handicap.—lleat winners J Roberts arnere Port), L Baldwin (St Helens), J C Shepherd 31:03 W Ward (Mouldsworth), A Hughes (Warring- and Jackson (Warrington). Final : 1, F Jack- L Baldwin; 3, A Hughes. Yards flat handicap.—Heat winners : N R (Frodsham), H Spruce (Halton), W Lodge agton). N Moore (Northwich) and C Roberts id). Final : 1, W Lodge; 2, H Spruce ; 3, N f-mile bicycle handicap.—Heats : James Wright E Corker (Frodsham), J Tudor (Whitby), .1 Helsby), J Ashley (Moulton) and T Dodd Final : 1, J Garner ; 2, J Ashley ;3, James Yards flat handicap.—Heat winners : W Lodge, F Jid White, R Baldwin, H Spruce and H Meals. 1, W Lodge; 2, F Lewis ; 3, J H White. •thile flat bandicap.—Final : 1, A Chorlton ; 2 ;3, H Wright. die bicycle handicap.—Heats : James Wright, ord, 3 Ashley,.] Darner and J Price. Final : 1, ; 2. James Wright; 3, J Garner. Tdri fiat handicap.—Heats : A Clforlton (North- Burgess (Davenham), C H Wright (Barnton), avies. R N Spencer and W Nelson (Weston). It Burgess ; 2, C H Wright ' • 3, E C Davies. tulle flit handicap.-1, A Lewis; 2, James Mercer ;3, A Potts (Aston). tuiles bicycle handicap.-1, James Wright ;2, J ; 3, J Ashley.</p>
