        <head>RESIGNATION OF CHIEF LIBERAL WHIP.</head>
        <p>RESIGNATION OF CHIEF LIBERAL WHIP.</p>
        <p>-- • It is officially announced that the Master of Elibank has resigned the position of Parliamentary Secretary to the Treasury and his seat in the House of Commons and has been made a peer. In a letter to the Midlothian Liberal Association the Chief Whip explains that his resignation is due to the great strain which has been imposed upon him by the duties of his office. He adds that he has accepted a partnership in the business of his old friend Lord Cowdray (Sir Weetman Pearson) Mr. Percy Illingworth succeeds the Master of Elibank as Chief Whip.</p>
