        <p>Peter Peacock Challenge Cup. The competition for this much coveted trophy is now rapidly coming to a finish and on Saturday the semi-final games were decided. As we predicted a few weeks ago the finalists site St. Austin's B and Town Ball A and when they meet in the final a keen tussle is expected. The games on Saturday were most interesting and the Town Ball men only managed to win by three chalks after a very exciting game. ST. JOHN'S D V. ST. AUSTIN'S B. The St. John's men only won on three individual games and the majority of the wins of their opponents were very decisive ones. One of the best games - of the match was the one between J Parr and J Howard, the latter only winning by two points in 19 ends. Howard had a slight advan- tage up to the 14th end, when the tables were turned and led 10-8. The players peeled with 10 each on the next end, and at the 18th end the score was 12-11 in favour of Howard, the St Austin's man, who eventually won 13-11. -- After having been in arrears 1-10 at the Bth end in his game with W Massey, W Critchley (St Johns) got the block and with a good run of 0 brought his score to 10-12 The St Austins player, however, got his winner on the next end and won by three points. -- wnrrEcnoss R V TOWN HALL A. There are some good bowlers included in both these teams and five of the Town Hall team gained run-away wins,these being E A Sanders,W Patrick (Captain) W H Dutton, J Collins, and J Groark who won over T Welsby, F Cleaton T Richardson, W Bibby, and E Williams 13-5, 13-2,13-8, 13-9 and 13-5 respectively in 16, 11, 16, 18, and 15 ends. -- R H Ilalford (Town Hall) bad hard lock in his game with F Davenport to lose 10-13 in the 16 ends. Although the Whitecross man showed splendid form, especially in the latter stages of the game. P Wright scored the highest number of points for a loser on the Whitecross side, and only lost 11-13 to 13 Webb in 19 ends, the game having beau 10-3 at one stage. The other games were fairly interesting, and a good afternoon wan spent. The final will take plaae on Saturday next. A number of gamea in the individual merit competi- tion will be played ttt-day, a lull list of which we gave last week. The games for next Saturday :have been postponed on account ot the lb al and Ea list of games for the 24th will be given in next Saturday's " Examiner."</p>
