        <p>SIR JOHN HANDLES ELECTED. Big Conservative majority, _— Polling for Oro election of a member for the North- west division of Manche,ter in the r ootn of Sir Ueorge Kemp, resigned, took place on Thursday. The result was decla•ed at nine &amp;clock as follows : Sir John S. Randles (C) 5 573 Mr. Gordon Hewart (L) _4.371 --- Conservative Majotity 1,202 There are 12,113 electors on the register. An analyeis cf the figures as cotnpared with those of the last poll in December, 1910,gives the following results : It crease in total electorate lB2 Decrease in total p01l Ir crease in Conservative poll 459 Decrease in Liberal poll PREVIOUS RESULTS. From 1885 to 1900 North-West Manchester returned a Conservative—Sir William liouldsworth— without a break. At the general election in 1892 at,d again in</p>
        <p>1900 he had no opposition. and at the other three elections, 1885, 1886 and 1895, his majorities were 723, 1030 and 1,471. The results of the four elections which have been held since 1900 were as follows : 1910 (December.) S.r George Kemp (L) 5,550 A Boner Law (0) 5,114 --- Liberal majority 415 1910 (January). Sir George Kemp (L) 5,930 W. Joynion Hicks (C) 5,147 --- Liberal Mak ity 783 10CtS (I3y-,lection ott Mr. Churchill's appo'utment as President of the Boai d of Trad W. Jo3nson-Hicks (C) 5,417 W. Churchill (L) D. Irving (Soo.) 275 --- Cons: majo-ity over Lib'l 429 1906. W. Churchill (L) 5,039 NV. Joynsou-Hicks (C) 4,398 Liberal majority 1,241 •</p>
